<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>UI Controls Demo</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f8f9fa;
      color: #333;
      line-height: 1.6;
      padding: 20px;
    }
    h1, h2 {
      color: #222;
    }
    section {
      background: white;
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 20px;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
    }
    .example {
      margin: 10px 0;
      padding: 10px;
      background: #f1f1f1;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }
    label {
      margin-right: 10px;
    }
    .tabs {
      display: flex;
      border-bottom: 2px solid #ccc;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .tab {
      padding: 10px 20px;
      border: 1px solid #ccc;
      border-bottom: none;
      border-radius: 10px 10px 0 0;
      background: #eee;
      margin-right: 5px;
    }
    .tab.active {
      background: white;
      font-weight: bold;
    }
    .tab-content {
      display: none;
      padding: 15px;
      border: 1px solid #ccc;
      border-top: none;
      background: white;
    }
    .tab-content.active {
      display: block;
    }
    .tooltip {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-block;
      cursor: help;
    }
    .tooltip .tooltiptext {
      visibility: hidden;
      width: 160px;
      background-color: #333;
      color: #fff;
      text-align: center;
      border-radius: 5px;
      padding: 5px;
      position: absolute;
      z-index: 1;
      bottom: 125%;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
      opacity: 0;
      transition: opacity 0.3s;
    }
    .tooltip:hover .tooltiptext {
      visibility: visible;
      opacity: 1;
    }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }
    th, td {
      border: 1px solid #ddd;
      padding: 8px;
    }
    th {
      background: #e9ecef;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>UI Controls Demonstration</h1>
  <p>This page shows and describes 10 common types of UI controls with examples.</p>

  <section id="radiobutton">
    <h2>1. Radio Button</h2>
    <p>Radio buttons allow the user to select <strong>only one option</strong> from a group.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <label><input type="radio" name="color" value="red"> Red</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="color" value="blue"> Blue</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="color" value="green"> Green</label>
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <label><input type="radio" name="size" value="s"> Small</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="size" value="m"> Medium</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="size" value="l"> Large</label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="checkbox">
    <h2>2. Checkbox</h2>
    <p>Checkboxes allow the user to select <strong>multiple options</strong> independently.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <label><input type="checkbox" /> HTML</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" /> CSS</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" /> JavaScript</label>
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <label><input type="checkbox" /> Receive newsletter</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" /> Accept terms</label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="textinput">
    <h2>3. Text Input</h2>
    <p>Used to enter text information such as name or email.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <input type="text" placeholder="Enter your name">
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <input type="email" placeholder="Enter your email">
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <input type="password" placeholder="Enter your password">
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="tabs">
    <h2>4. Tabs</h2>
    <p>Tabs allow the user to switch between different views or content panels.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="tabs">
        <div class="tab active" data-target="tab1">HTML</div>
        <div class="tab" data-target="tab2">CSS</div>
        <div class="tab" data-target="tab3">JS</div>
      </div>
      <div id="tab1" class="tab-content active">HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.</div>
      <div id="tab2" class="tab-content">CSS styles the appearance of web pages.</div>
      <div id="tab3" class="tab-content">JavaScript adds interactivity to web pages.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="button">
    <h2>5. Button</h2>
    <p>Buttons trigger an action when clicked.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <button onclick="alert('You clicked me!')">Click Me</button>
      <button disabled>Disabled Button</button>
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <button style="background: #28a745; color: white; border: none; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 5px;">Submit</button>
      <button style="background: #dc3545; color: white; border: none; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 5px;">Cancel</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="label">
    <h2>6. Text Label</h2>
    <p>Labels describe or identify other elements, like input fields.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <label for="username">Username:</label>
      <input id="username" type="text">
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <label for="age">Age:</label>
      <input id="age" type="number" min="1" max="120">
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="link">
    <h2>7. Link</h2>
    <p>Links navigate the user to another page or section.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <a href="https://www.google.com" target="_blank">Go to Google</a>
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <a href="#radiobutton">Jump to Radio Button section</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="tooltip">
    <h2>8. Tooltip</h2>
    <p>Tooltips show helpful information when hovering over an element.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="tooltip">Hover over me
        <span class="tooltiptext">This is a tooltip message!</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="tooltip">Info
        <span class="tooltiptext">Tooltips are great for hints!</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="dropdown">
    <h2>9. Dropdown List</h2>
    <p>Dropdown lists let the user select one value from a list of options.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <select>
        <option>Choose a country</option>
        <option>Ukraine</option>
        <option>Poland</option>
        <option>Germany</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <select>
        <option>Select fruit</option>
        <option>Apple</option>
        <option>Banana</option>
        <option>Orange</option>
      </select>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="datagrid">
    <h2>10. Data Grid (Table)</h2>
    <p>A data grid displays data in tabular form, often sortable or searchable.</p>
    <div class="example">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Age</th><th>Country</th></tr>
        <tr><td>John</td><td>25</td><td>USA</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Olga</td><td>30</td><td>Ukraine</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mark</td><td>22</td><td>UK</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Product</th><th>Price</th><th>In Stock</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Laptop</td><td>$800</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Phone</td><td>$500</td><td>No</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tablet</td><td>$300</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    // Tabs functionality
    document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(tab => {
      tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
        document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(t => t.classList.remove('active'));
        document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content').forEach(c => c.classList.remove('active'));
        tab.classList.add('active');
        document.getElementById(tab.dataset.target).classList.add('active');
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
